{
    "post_id": 67663,
    "title": "A Blessing Before a Dyke March, by Anastasia bat Lilith",
    "author": "Anastasia bat Lilith",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Anastasia bat Lilith",
            "bio": "Anastasia bat Lilith (<span class=\"hebrew\">אַנאַסטאַסיאַ בת לילית</span>) is a transfemme Jewish Anarcha-Feminist living in Diondega, so-called \"Pittsburgh, PA\". Zine queen, librarian and one-time exorcist, she helps organize the Pittsburgh Jewish Zine Fest and Ratzon: Center for Healing and Resistance. She loves long walks on the beach, and unicorns.",
            "website": "http://linktr.ee/stormbringerpress",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/anastasia-bat-lilith-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/anastasia-bat-lilith"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-06-07",
    "last_updated": "2026-07-29",
    "excerpt": "A poem / blessing made for the 2026 Pittsburgh Dyke March, framed with a Hebrew blessing for Lesbian Pride written by Rabbi Robin Podolsky.",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nA poem / blessing made for the 2026 Pittsburgh Dyke March, framed with a Hebrew blessing for Lesbian Pride written by Rabbi Robin Podolsky.\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\"><a href=\"/translate/\" target=\"_blank\">Contribute&nbsp;a&nbsp;translation</a></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Source (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWe&#8217;re not here for equality,<br />\nbut Liberation.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWe march for solidarity,<br />\nto pray with our feet,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Rabbi Dr. Abraham Joshua Heschel on March 21, 1965 after returning from participating in the Selma-to-Montgomery March: “For many of us the march from Selma to Montgomery was about protest and prayer. Legs are not lips and walking is not kneeling. And yet our legs uttered songs. Even without words, our march was worship. I felt my legs were praying.”&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> and<br />\nput commitments to action.</p>\n<p>We march for our ancestors,<br />\nfinding joy in the world they bled for.\n</p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nEvery dyke, trannie and freak beaten<br />\nor jailed by The State is my comrade.</p>\n<p>Every queer killed for their identity<br />\nis my sibling, their loss my own.</p>\n<p>Will we be mere allies,<br />\nor accomplices to their memory?\n</p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWe march knowing our liberation is bound<br />\nup in each other.</p>\n<p>We march not merely as friends, but lovers.\n</p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWhere do we belong, love?<br />\nWE BELONG TO THE FUTURE!</p>\n<p>Let us make ourselves holy, and live<br />\nlike that better world is here for the taking!\n</p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nבְּרוּכָה אַתְ יָהּ<br />\nאוֹהֶבֶת הָעוֹלָם<br />\nהַלֵב הַפּוֹעֵם שֶׁל כֹּל הָעוֹלָמוֹת<br />\nבּוֹרֵאת צְחוֹקָן שֶׁל כַּלּוֹת<br />\nוּשְׂשׂוֹנָן שֶׁל שֻׁתָפוֹת לְמַאֲבָק<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Hebrew blessing as written by Rabbi Robin Podolsky in <em><a href=\"https://www.ccarpress.org/9780881233582/mishkan-gaavah-where-pride-dwells/\">Mishkan Ga&#8217;avah Where Pride Dwells</a></em> (CCAR: 2019).&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"romanized-transliteration\" lang=\"heb-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nBrukhah ăt Yah<br />\nōhevet ha’ōlăm<br />\nhalév hapō&#8217;ém shel kōl ha’ōlamōt<br />\nborét ts&#8217;ḥōqăn shel kalōt<br />\nus’sōnăn shel shūtăfōt l’maăvăq.\n</div>\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Yah</span>,<br />\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">Lover of the universe</span>,<br />\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">Heartbeat of the worlds</span>,<br />\nwho has made the laughter of brides<br />\nand the joy of comrades.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<p>This prayer was offered by Anastasia bat Lilith at the <a href=\"https://qburgh.com/event/pgh-dyke-march/\">Pittsburg Dyke March</a> on 6 June 2026 in Friendship Park. The concluding blessing, by Rabbi Robin Podolsky, was first published in <em><a href=\"https://www.ccarpress.org/9780881233582/mishkan-gaavah-where-pride-dwells/\">Mishkan Ga&#8217;avah Where Pride Dwells</a></em> (CCAR: 2019).</p>\n<div class=\"speaker-mute footnotes_reference_container\"> <div class=\"footnote_container_prepare\"><p><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_label pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\">Notes</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_collapse_button\" style=\"display: none;; display: none;\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\"></span></p></div> <div id=\"footnote_references_container__1\" style=\"\"><table class=\"footnotes_table footnote-reference-container\"><caption class=\"accessibility\">Notes</caption> <tbody> \r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >1</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Rabbi Dr. Abraham Joshua Heschel on March 21, 1965 after returning from participating in the Selma-to-Montgomery March: “For many of us the march from Selma to Montgomery was about protest and prayer. Legs are not lips and walking is not kneeling. And yet our legs uttered songs. Even without words, our march was worship. I felt my legs were praying.”</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >2</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Hebrew blessing as written by Rabbi Robin Podolsky in <em><a href=\"https://www.ccarpress.org/9780881233582/mishkan-gaavah-where-pride-dwells/\">Mishkan Ga&#8217;avah Where Pride Dwells</a></em> (CCAR: 2019).</td></tr>\r\n\r\n </tbody> </table> </div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\"> function footnote_expand_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').show(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('−'); } function footnote_collapse_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').hide(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('+'); } function footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1() { if (jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').is(':hidden')) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); } else { footnote_collapse_reference_container__1(); } } function footnote_moveToReference__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } } function footnote_moveToAnchor__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } }</script>",
